{"id":"55b1d917f2b95856","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-diaconescu.md","title":"Diaconescu's Theorem","display":"thm-diaconescu — Diaconescu's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-diaconescu","aliases":["58-thm-diaconescu"],"display":"thm-diaconescu — Diaconescu's Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-diaconescu"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-diaconescu</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-diaconescu — Diaconescu's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6ea17c91dcff1011\" href=\"?note=6ea17c91dcff1011\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md\">../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IZF}\">\\(\\mathrm{IZF}\\)</span> (intuitionistic set theory used as the ambient theory)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AC}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AC}_S\\)</span> (axiom-of-choice proposition, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"6ea17c91dcff1011\" href=\"?note=6ea17c91dcff1011\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md\">../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> is an arbitrary sentence of the object language of IZF (a metasyntactic parameter)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_p,B_p,c\\in V\">\\(A_p,B_p,c\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu}(p) \\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\\to(p\\lor\\neg p).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu}(p) \\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\\to(p\\lor\\neg p).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu\\text{-}choice\\text{-}data}(p)\\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\nA_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}\\land B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}\\land\\mathrm{AC}_S\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists c\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(c,\\{A_p,B_p\\},\\bigcup\\{A_p,B_p\\}\\bigr)\n\\land c(A_p)\\in A_p\\land c(B_p)\\in B_p\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\land(c(A_p)=c(B_p)\\to p)\n\\land(c(A_p)\\neq c(B_p)\\to\\neg p)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu\\text{-}choice\\text{-}data}(p)\\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\nA_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}\\land B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}\\land\\mathrm{AC}_S\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists c\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(c,\\{A_p,B_p\\},\\bigcup\\{A_p,B_p\\}\\bigr)\n\\land c(A_p)\\in A_p\\land c(B_p)\\in B_p\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\land(c(A_p)=c(B_p)\\to p)\n\\land(c(A_p)\\neq c(B_p)\\to\\neg p)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For the metasyntactic sentence <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>, set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}\">\\(A_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}\">\\(B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}\\)</span>. Choice is applied to the set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{A_p,B_p\\}\">\\(\\{A_p,B_p\\}\\)</span> itself, so if <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> makes <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_p=B_p\">\\(A_p=B_p\\)</span>, functionality forces the two selected values to agree.</li>\n<li>Decidable equality on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> gives two cases: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a_p=b_p\">\\(a_p=b_p\\)</span> implies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>, while <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a_p\\neq b_p\">\\(a_p\\neq b_p\\)</span> implies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg p\">\\(\\neg p\\)</span> because <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> would make <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_p=B_p\">\\(A_p=B_p\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Since <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> was arbitrary, this theorem schema says that full choice over IZF entails excluded middle.  It does not quantify over a nonexistent object-language set of all propositions.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md","status":"resolved","id":"6ea17c91dcff1011","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md","status":"resolved","id":"6ea17c91dcff1011","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AC}_S$ (axiom-of-choice proposition, see [[../batch14/58-df-axiom-of-choice.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{IZF}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AC}_S","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"A_p,B_p,c\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu}(p) \\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\n\\mathrm{AC}_S\\to(p\\lor\\neg p).","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}diaconescu\\text{-}choice\\text{-}data}(p)\\vdash_{\\mathrm{IZF}}\nA_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}\\land B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}\\land\\mathrm{AC}_S\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\\exists c\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(c,\\{A_p,B_p\\},\\bigcup\\{A_p,B_p\\}\\bigr)\n\\land c(A_p)\\in A_p\\land c(B_p)\\in B_p\\\\\n&\\hspace{9em}\\land(c(A_p)=c(B_p)\\to p)\n\\land(c(A_p)\\neq c(B_p)\\to\\neg p)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"A_p=\\{0\\}\\cup\\{1:p\\}","display":false},{"tex":"B_p=\\{1\\}\\cup\\{0:p\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\{A_p,B_p\\}","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"A_p=B_p","display":false},{"tex":"\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"a_p=b_p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"a_p\\neq b_p","display":false},{"tex":"\\neg p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"A_p=B_p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false}],"bytes":1732,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4117","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-thm-diaconescu.md|58-thm-diaconescu]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["6ea17c91dcff1011","36d7463d215be751"]}